    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#korea">Korea</a>'s longest-ruling dynasty, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#taejo-of-joseon">Yi Seong-gye</a> in 1392 and ruled from Hanseong, today's Seoul.</li><li>A model Neo-Confucian state run by examination-trained yangban officials; King Sejong created the Korean alphabet in 1443.</li><li>It survived Japanese and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#manchus">Manchu</a> invasions but was forced open by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#japan">Japan</a> in 1876 and became the Korean Empire in 1897.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Annals of the Joseon Dynasty record 472 years of government day by day, written by court historians whose drafts even the king was not supposed to read.</p></aside>
    </section>

